It is Sunday morning.
I make a video call to my family in Mexico.
My younger sister Sofia answers the phone.
"Are you well, sister?" she asks.
"I am well," I say.
I turn the camera towards Tommy.
Tommy is sleeping on his bed.
"Sofia, look."
"This is Tommy," I say.
"He is very cute to look at," Sofia says.
"He is my neighbour Anitha's dog," I explain.
"I must look after him this weekend."
"I must give him food on time."
"I must not give him sweet snacks."
Then Sofia brings our dog Lola in front of the camera.
Lola sees Tommy on the phone screen.
Immediately, she barks loudly.
Hearing that sound, Tommy wakes up suddenly.
Tommy also barks back.
"Tommy, sit!"
"You must not make noise," I tell him.
He sits obediently beside me.
"He is a good boy."
"I like him very much," I tell Sofia.
